>39</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8421494</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005876-Martin1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Grimwood</surname><given-names>PD</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Synaptic plasticity and memory: an evaluation of the hypothesis.</article-title><source>Annu Rev Neurosci</source><volume>23</volume><fpage>649</fpage><lpage>711</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10845078</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005876-Mulkey1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mulkey</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Malenka</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Mechanisms underlying induction of homosynaptic long-term depression in area CA1 of the hippocampus.</article-title><source>Neuron</source><volume>9</volume><fpage>967</fpage><lpage>975</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1419003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005876-Bliss2"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bliss</surname><given-names>TV</given-names></name><name><surname>Lomo</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>1973</year><article-title>Long-lasting potentiation of synaptic transmission in the dentate area of the anaesthetized rabbit following stimulation of the perforant path.</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><volume>232</volume><fpage>331</fpage><lpage>356</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4727084</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005876-Malenka1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malenka</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Bear</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>LTP and LTD: an embarrassment of riches.</article-title><source>Neuron</source><volume>44</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15450156</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005876-Squire1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Squire</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Memory and the hippocampus: a synthesis from findings with rats, monkeys, and humans.</article-title><source>Psychol Rev</source><volume>99</volume><fpage>195</fpage><lpage>231</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1594723</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005876-Malenka2"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malenka</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Nicoll</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Long-term potentiation-a decade of progress?</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>285</volume><fpage>1870</fpage><lpage>1874</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10489359</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0005876-Zhang2"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanswell</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Luo</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>The effects of bilirubin on evoked potentials and long-term potentiation in rat hippocampus <italic>in vivo</italic>.</article-title><source>Pediatr Res</source><volume>53</volume><fpage>939</fpage><lpage>944</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12621100</